   <ComplexType hideInDiagrams="false"
                name="IdentifiedObject"
                ea_guid="EAID_055C5806_E9D8_4a7a_9307_DAF7C31763C7"
                baseClass="http://iec.ch/TC57/CIM-generic#IdentifiedObject"
                package="Core"
                packageURI="http://iec.ch/TC57/CIM-generic#Package_Core"
                minOccurs="0"
                maxOccurs="unbounded">
      <Comment>This is a root class to provide common identification for all classes needing identification and naming attributes.</Comment>
      <AsciiDoc xml:space="preserve">The type of a transformer is derived as follows:</AsciiDoc>
      <AsciiDoc xml:space="preserve"/>
      <AsciiDoc xml:space="preserve">[source,python]</AsciiDoc>
      <AsciiDoc xml:space="preserve">----</AsciiDoc>
      <AsciiDoc xml:space="preserve">If PowerTransformer.EquipmentContainer-&gt; EquipmentContainer.@type:</AsciiDoc>
      <AsciiDoc xml:space="preserve">    xfmerType = DCConverterUnit # see DCConverterUnit</AsciiDoc>
      <AsciiDoc xml:space="preserve">else:</AsciiDoc>
      <AsciiDoc xml:space="preserve">    count = PowerTransformer.count(PowerTransformerEnd)</AsciiDoc>
      <AsciiDoc xml:space="preserve">    if count == 2:</AsciiDoc>
      <AsciiDoc xml:space="preserve">        xfmerType = TwoWinding</AsciiDoc>
      <AsciiDoc xml:space="preserve">    elif count == 3:</AsciiDoc>
      <AsciiDoc xml:space="preserve">        xfmerType = ThreeWinding</AsciiDoc>
      <AsciiDoc xml:space="preserve">    else:</AsciiDoc>
      <AsciiDoc xml:space="preserve">        # Log error</AsciiDoc>
      <AsciiDoc xml:space="preserve">----</AsciiDoc>
      <Simple hideInDiagrams="false"
              name="mRID"
              xstype="string"
              dataType="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"
              cimDatatype="http://iec.ch/TC57/CIM-generic#String"
              ea_guid="EAID_C775F80A_A23D_4f38_AB9D_49D1FA882337"
              baseProperty="http://iec.ch/TC57/CIM-generic#IdentifiedObject.mRID"
              basePropertyClass="http://iec.ch/TC57/CIM-generic#IdentifiedObject"
              minOccurs="1"
              maxOccurs="1">
         <Comment>Master resource identifier issued by a model authority. The mRID is unique within an exchange context. Global uniqueness is easily achieved by using a UUID, as specified in RFC 4122, for the mRID. The use of UUID is strongly recommended.</Comment>
         <Comment>For CIMXML data files in RDF syntax conforming to IEC 61970-552, the mRID is mapped to rdf:ID or rdf:about attributes that identify CIM object elements.</Comment>
         <Stereotype label="Attribute">http://langdale.com.au/2005/UML#attribute</Stereotype>
      </Simple>
      <Simple hideInDiagrams="false"
              name="name"
              xstype="string"
